From 1ccbe39e4b8079c8a81dc2b315241fe68b727af1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:39:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Seccomp: only the trap's own SIGSYS resumes past the trapped
 syscall

The SECCOMP_RET_TRAP path records the address after the syscall in
the thread (SeccompTrapRIP) and the next guest signal frame takes it.
An asynchronous signal arriving between the filter's decision and the
SIGSYS delivery (Wine signalling a thread for NtGetContextThread or an
APC while it is in its SIGSYS syscall dispatcher) took it instead: its
handler returned past the syscall and the trap was skipped, the SIGSYS
never reaching the guest. Only a SIGSYS with si_code SYS_SECCOMP
consumes the address now.

Upstream state: SeccompTrapRIP comes from this branch's 'Seccomp:
report SECCOMP_RET_TRAP at the instruction after the syscall'; FEX
main has no such field.

Test: eac-tests/signal-race (new check 'every trapped syscall
delivered exactly one SIGSYS'): eac-2610 loses SIGSYS in 14 of 60 runs
on a Neoverse N2 runner (up to 483 of 488 traps), 0 of 60 with this
change; native x86-64 30/30.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp     | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp
index 07af884..451801c 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SignalDelegator.cpp
@@ -333,8 +333,13 @@ bool SignalDelegator::HandleDispatcherGuestSignal(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadS
   // itself, so the ucontext RIP now differs from it: rt_sigreturn then takes the path that restores the handler's
   // registers and resumes at the ucontext RIP, instead of the path that resets to the interrupted state and re-runs
   // the syscall (discarding the handler's return value). See SeccompEmulator for the kernel semantics.
-  ContextBackup->SeccompTrapRIP = ThreadObject->SeccompTrapRIP;
-  ThreadObject->SeccompTrapRIP = 0;
+  // Only the trap's own SIGSYS takes it: an asynchronous signal that arrives between the filter deciding to trap and
+  // the SIGSYS being delivered must see the interrupted state (RIP at the `syscall`), otherwise its handler returns
+  // past the syscall and the trap is skipped without its SIGSYS ever reaching the guest.
+  if (Signal == SIGSYS && static_cast<siginfo_t*>(info)->si_code == 1 /* SYS_SECCOMP */) {
+    ContextBackup->SeccompTrapRIP = ThreadObject->SeccompTrapRIP;
+    ThreadObject->SeccompTrapRIP = 0;
+  }
   ContextBackup->SavedJITStackSP = ThreadObject->JITStackSP;
 
   auto Frame = Thread->CurrentFrame;
